Subject: Re: Next steps — SDK gateway and endpoint migration plan

Great — Option A confirmed. Below are the concrete technical recommendations for Languora's integration and migration. I pasted short SDK examples and endpoint mapping to make the handoff turnkey.

1) Sandbox vs Prod endpoints
- Sandbox (use during initial integration and load tests): https://sandbox.api.redwood.ai/v1/generate
- Prod (gateway-managed): https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate
- During shadow: traffic should POST to the prod endpoint but include header X-Redwood-Shadow: languora to avoid billing and enable traffic tagging.

2) Recommended client settings (based on your profile)
- Connection timeout: 2s
- Read/socket timeout: 15s (given 240 token avg completion)
- Retries: 2 application-level idempotent retries with exponential backoff (200ms -> 600ms), preserve request body and discourage replays for non-idempotent calls.
- Circuit breaker: open after 25% error rate for 60s; we can tune during shadow.

3) Sample Node.js snippet (SDK-based retry wrapper)

const Redwood = require('@redwood-inference/sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY, baseUrl: 'https://sandbox.api.redwood.ai/v1' });

async function callGenerate(payload) {
  let attempts = 0;
  while (attempts < 3) {
    try {
      attempts++;
      const res = await client.generate(payload, { timeout: 15000 });
      return res;
    } catch (err) {
      if (attempts >= 3) throw err;
      const delay = 200 * Math.pow(3, attempts - 1);
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));
    }
  }
}

Note: above uses the SDK to handle auth and streaming — prefer using the provided client to avoid mistakes around KV cache headers and model variant negotiation.

4) Migration plan (high level)
- Sandbox integration: Mar 26–28 — basic calls + load test.
- Shadow traffic: Apr 4–5 — route prod traffic with X-Redwood-Shadow header, monitor latency, token counts, and error rates.
- Incremental ramp: Apr 6 — 0% -> 10% -> 25% -> 50% -> 100% across 6 hours with rollback gates at each step.

5) Observability hooks (what we'll need from Languora)
- Request IDs in logs, average tokens per request metric, and any business KPI signals for quality checks.

Attachments: updated migration-checklist.xlsx (I added the Node snippet + timeline). I'll upload the SDK samples to the shared drive and DM the link once available.

If you want, Samir can host a 60-minute technical walkthrough with your infra team on Mon/Mar 25.

